 "equipment_type": "VAV terminal unit controller",
 "applies_to": "Nailor VAV terminal units with EZvav digital controls: BAC-8001-36 (cooling only), BAC-8005-36 and BAC-8205-36 (fan and reheat) and BAC-8007-36 (dual duct).",
 "summary": "EZvav is Nailor's factory-mounted VAV controller family, BTL-listed BACnet application specific controllers on BACnet MS/TP (up to 76.8 kbaud). Device instance, MAC and baud are set from the STE-8001W36 wall sensor without software. The object list covers space temperature and setpoints, occupied and unoccupied cooling and heating setpoints, airflow limits and calibration, fan and reheat outputs, discharge air control, AHU request flags, occupancy mode and the cooling, heating and DAT loops.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "The controllers are KMC SimplyVAV models sold under the Nailor EZvav name; the list matches KMC's SimplyVAV list apart from a few names (e.g. AV 2 STPT REFERENCE, AV 12 STBY DIFF, AI 3 SPACE SET POINT) and a few objects KMC adds (AV 51, AV 54).",
  "The manual gives object, name and description only. Access is inferred: setpoint and configuration AVs writable, inputs, outputs and calculated values read-only.",
  "Not every object exists on every model; AV 48-50 are BAC-8205-36 only.",
  "Multistate values are printed as MSV1-MSV6 and loops as LOOP1-LOOP3; they are listed as MV and LO objects.",
  "BV 3 is printed with the description 'Need For AHU' (same as BV 1) and MSV 6 as 'Multi-state Value #6'.",
  "Source: BACnet objects, manual pages 44-46 (74 objects)."
 ],
